@startuml
title Planned sequence — History, stored result and analyst note
hide footbox
autonumber

actor "Fraud Prevention Analyst" as Analyst
participant "React web app\n[planned]" as Web
participant "nginx\n[planned]" as Nginx
participant "FastAPI\n[skeleton implemented]" as API
database "SQLite metadata\n[planned]" as DB

Analyst -> Web: Open History
Web -> Web: Restore verdict/date/query/page\nfrom URL and scroll from history state
Web -> Nginx: GET /api/analyses?filters&page
Nginx -> API: Proxy request
API -> DB: Query newest-first records and counts

alt Query or storage failure
  DB --> API: Failure
  API --> Nginx: Structured 400 or 500 error
  Nginx --> Web: Error
  Web --> Analyst: History failed state and Retry
else Query succeeds
  DB --> API: items, total, page, page_size, counts
  API --> Nginx: 200 paged response
  Nginx --> Web: Paged History
  alt No matching records
    Web --> Analyst: Empty or filtered-empty state
  else Records available
    Web --> Analyst: Table/cards with verdict, risk and time
    Analyst -> Web: Open request_id
    Web -> Nginx: GET /api/analyses/{request_id}
    Nginx -> API: Proxy request
    API -> DB: Read analysis and separate note
    alt Unknown request_id
      DB --> API: Not found
      API --> Nginx: 404 not_found
      Nginx --> Web: Structured error
      Web --> Analyst: Unknown request message
    else Stored result found
      DB --> API: StoredAnalysis
      API --> Nginx: 200 StoredAnalysis
      Nginx --> Web: Analysis plus optional note
      Web --> Analyst: Details and decision-support notice

      opt Analyst adds, replaces or removes note
        Analyst -> Web: Save note text
        Web -> Nginx: PUT /api/analyses/{request_id}/note
        Nginx -> API: Proxy note request
        API -> API: Trim and validate note_max_chars
        alt Invalid note or write failure
          API --> Nginx: Structured 400, 404 or 500 error
          Nginx --> Web: Error
          Web --> Analyst: Keep draft and show not-saved state
        else Valid note
          API -> DB: Upsert note, or delete if text is empty
          DB --> API: Updated Note or null
          API --> Nginx: 200 note response
          Nginx --> Web: Note saved/removed
          Web --> Analyst: Saved confirmation
        end
      end
    end
  end
end

note over Web,DB
  The note never changes the immutable analysis result.
  History stores metadata only; audio is never persisted.
end note
@enduml
